course: dictionary
lesson: 3878
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one. The word free is a good example. «Borrowing books from the public library is free» means it costs no money. The words around it are about money, so free means you pay nothing.
explain: Look at this sentence: «None of these machines gives energy for free.» Here free means without paying, and it sits in the phrase for free. Ask yourself what the sentence needs, then put your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Free can also mean not busy or not shut in. «I have free time after school» means I have nothing I must do. «Set free» means let go, so a trapped animal is freed. When you meet free, read the words near it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Free means it costs no money: you pay nothing for it.
fact: Free can mean not shut in or held, so a free bird can fly where it wants.
fact: Free time is time with nothing you must do.
fact: To free someone or something is to let it go or get it loose.
fact: Free from and free of mean without something, like sugar-free or free of charge.
exercise: «Borrowing books from the public library is free.» What does free mean here? | *It costs no money | It is set loose from a cage | It is shut in and locked | It is very busy
exercise: «A trapped animal was freed and ran into the woods.» What does freed mean? | *Let go or got loose | Counted as zero | Made very busy | Paid for in full
exercise: «Sugar-free sweets have no sugar in them.» What does free mean in sugar-free? | *Without something, here without sugar | Costing nothing | Shut inside a box | Not busy
test: «I have free time after school, so I can read.» What does free time mean? | Time spent paying for things | *Time with nothing you must do | Time when the shops are shut | Time spent in a cage
test: «Buy two, get one free.» What does free mean here? | It is far away | It is shut in | *It costs nothing | It is very busy
exam: «The bus has a free seat by the window.» What does free mean? | Locked shut | *Empty and not being used | Costs money to sit in | Full of friends
